class:: SpecStrongPeak
summary:: Fraction of spectral mass in the strongest bin
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/SpecCentroid2, Classes/SpecFlatness2

description::
Returns max(w) / sum(w), between 0 and 1. This explicitly defines strongest-peak dominance as a bin concentration ratio; it is not the bandwidth-based StrongPeak formula used by some MIR libraries.

For these formulas w is the raw FFT magnitude or its square, and f is the bin-center frequency in Hz. Silence returns 0. The reader preserves the FFT chain. Independent maximum-to-sum concentration descriptor specified for MIRa.

CPU cost is linear in the number of FFT bins; no memory is allocated while processing. It adds no lookahead beyond the upstream FFT. At a 1024-sample window and 48 kHz the initial analysis window is about 21.3 ms. Changing FFT size or window affects unnormalized values.

Like vanilla link::Classes/SpecCentroid::, this reads FFT frames and produces control-rate timbre information; this class measures fraction of spectral mass in the strongest bin instead of the average frequency.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: chain
FFT chain from an FFT with the same literal fftSize. New-frame values update the output; between frames the previous output is retained.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included bin center in Hz; default 0 includes DC.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included bin center in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist. Empty ranges return 0.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 uses magnitude; literal 1 uses squared magnitude (power).

argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two from 256 through 8192. Must match the FFT buffer.

returns::
One control-rate descriptor value.

examples::
SpecStrongPeak measures the fraction of total spectral mass concentrated in the single strongest bin (between 0 and 1). Pure sinusoidal or resonant acoustic tones exhibit high concentration; broadband noise exhibits low concentration. In this example, strong peak concentration tunes the resonance Q of a tracking bandpass filter to accentuate vocal and instrumental formants. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time strong peak concentration.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var peakRatio = SpecStrongPeak.kr(chain, minFreq: 80, maxFreq: 8000, spectrumMode: 0, fftSize: 1024);
        var resQ = peakRatio.lag(0.08).linlin(0.05, 0.4, 0.5, 0.05).clip(0.05, 0.8);
        var filtered = BPF.ar(source, 1200, resQ) * 0.4;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + filtered;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, peakRatio.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Strong Peak Fraction", ~miraBus, 0.0, 0.5, "ratio");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
